  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After named Chernoff and dense-subgraph-to-hidden-clique reconstruction inputs, the new randomized payoff-block reduction must rule out concentrated small supports, convert near-optimal payoff into mass inside the graph block, and extract a dense logarithmic bipartite subgraph from an approximate equilibrium. All generalized parameter inequalities and the complete small-support/density proof are supplied before the eta-dependent completeness/soundness closing. This is one H2 planted-clique reduction rather than an ordinary equilibrium existence or concentration exercise.",
  "source_scope_note": "Exact original formal Theorem3.7 only: for each eta>0 the randomized polynomial-time game construction maps a hidden clique of C ln n vertices to an exact equilibrium of maximum average payoff alpha, and every (1/2-eta)-equilibrium within delta=Omega(eta^2) of that payoff allows polynomial-time clique recovery, with the source high-probability convention. Complete payoff matrices, newly generalized dense-subgraph extraction, small-set mass proof, mass-in-A and conditional-value support are retained. The cited HK11 dense-bipartite-subgraph recovery theorem and Chernoff–Hoeffding remain named prerequisites. Small-support, second-equilibrium, Bayesian and other parameter regimes are unselected references and not counted. All-page source/output QA completed; exact final actual logs have zero missing-glyph/reference/citation/stability/box or other warning lines. Source-material candidate only, no admission/remote-delivery credit.",
  "source_quirks_note": "The original small-support probability expressions in its two original displays contain beta to the negative |S| power inside 1 minus that term. Native source and published proof preserve these exact signs; no exponent or probability-expression correction, counterexample analysis or mathematical-refereeing conclusion is supplied.",
